{#- "Leave us a Google review" counter sign, shared by sign-review.njk (colour)
    and sign-review-bw.njk (`bw: true`). The QR encodes
    https://lvcafetogo.com/review (src/review.njk), which forwards to
    site.reviews.googleUrl, so a printed sign survives a change of that link.

    THE WORDING ASKS EVERYONE. Google allows asking for reviews, but not
    asking only the happy customers and not giving anything for one (its
    contribution policy, read 2026-10-30). So the sign says "good or bad",
    never "Enjoyed your visit?", and nothing is ever offered with it.

    THE STEPS are spelled out because this audience skews older: the camera
    is not an obvious place to start. The link opens the cafe's Google page,
    not a sign-in page (site.json, _comment_reviews). Google still wants an
    account to post one, so the foot gives anyone without one the paper card. -#}
<div class="canvas sign sign--review{% if bw %} sign--bw{% endif %}">
    {% include "partials/studio/sign-mast.njk" %}

    <div class="sign-heading">
        <h2 class="p-display sign-heading-title ink-teal">Leave us a Google review</h2>
        <p class="p-body sign-survey-sub">Good or bad, it helps people find us.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="sign-survey-qr">
        {% inlineSvg "/assets/qr-review.svg" %}
    </div>

    <ol class="p-body sign-review-steps">
        <li>Open your phone&rsquo;s camera and point it at the square</li>
        <li>Tap the link that pops up</li>
        <li>Scroll down to the stars, tap one, and write a few words</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="p-display sign-survey-url ink-teal">{{ site.social.website }}/review</p>

    <div class="sign-spacer"></div>
    <p class="p-body sign-foot">No Google account? Ask for a survey card at the counter.</p>
</div>
